Why Do Mature Nodes Remain Important?

Mature process nodes support many chips that do not require the smallest available transistor dimensions. Analog circuits, microcontrollers, display drivers, power-management ICs and mixed-signal devices often benefit more from specialized functions and manufacturing reliability than from migration to leading-edge logic processes.

Established process platforms also provide mature design tools, proven manufacturing histories and extensive intellectual-property ecosystems.

Automotive and Industrial Electronics Support Demand

Automotive and industrial applications often require long qualification cycles and extended product availability. These conditions favor stable manufacturing processes with proven reliability.

Electric vehicles, factory automation, connected devices and power electronics continue to create demand for chips produced using established and specialty process technologies.

Specialty Processes Add Strategic Value

Foundries differentiate themselves through technologies such as embedded non-volatile memory, radio-frequency processes, high-voltage devices, image sensors and power-management platforms.

The market therefore extends beyond basic wafer production. Process integration, design support, reliability and long-term capacity commitments are important competitive factors.

